course: dictionary
lesson: 3299
title: Big words for big ideas
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eternity is a noun, and it means time that goes on for ever, with no end. Some people use it about life after death, which they believe never ends. You can read the words around it to check: «I waited an eternity for the bus.» Nobody waits for ever, so an eternity here means a very long time that feels endless.
explain: Eternity is one of the words people use to exaggerate. This is called hyperbole. When you say «I waited an eternity», you are not giving a measurement. You are telling the listener that the wait felt much too long.
explain: Words from other languages often mean the same thing. In Ukrainian, «Чекаю цілу вічність» (Chekayu tsilu vichnist) means «I've been waiting a whole eternity», which is the same idea as English «forever». Ask yourself what the sentence is trying to say, and the meaning will usually come to you.
fact: Eternity means time that goes on for ever, with no end.
fact: In church and religion, eternity can mean the life after death that believers think never ends.
fact: «For all eternity» means for ever.
fact: «An eternity» is an informal way of saying a very long time, as in «I waited an eternity for the bus.»
fact: Eternity is uncountable when you mean time for ever, but you can say an eternity or eternities for a long wait.
exercise: «I waited an eternity for the bus.» What does an eternity mean here? | A bus stop painted blue | *A very long time, though the wait was not really endless | A short bus ride to the park | A bus with no wheels
exercise: Which word means time that goes on for ever, with no end? | Holiday | *Eternity | Birthday | Sunrise
exercise: The Ukrainian «Чекаю цілу вічність» means «I've been waiting a whole eternity». Which English word is closest in meaning? | Yesterday | Quickly | Nearby | *Forever
test: In church and religion, what can eternity mean? | *The life after death that believers think never ends | A hymn book | The Sunday service | A type of church bell
test: What does «for all eternity» mean? | Until lunchtime | For a short while | For one hour only | *For ever, with no end
exam: Why do people say «I waited an eternity» when they were not really waiting for ever? | *It is hyperbole, an exaggeration to show that the wait felt very long | Because buses never come | Because they are very tired | Because eternity is a number on the clock
